# DTF tier manifest: download-route-token-basic
#   (artifact-keeper#4654 fixing #4593, and #4550; both in 1.11.1, RED on 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. Both fixes are in the HTTP auth layer and
# the admin handlers, ahead of storage.
#
# THE BUGS
#   #4593 / #4654  GET /api/v1/repositories/{key}/download/{path} answered a
#          request with no credential on a private repository with the
#          existence-hiding 404 and no WWW-Authenticate challenge, so clients
#          that send credentials only after a challenge (wget, curl without
#          pre-auth, Maven) never sent them. The route also sat under the
#          /api/v1 Basic boundary (#2809), so `user:<api_token>` was refused
#          401 even when sent. Fixed: no credential on a non-public or missing
#          repository -> 401 with Basic and Bearer challenges (byte-identical
#          for the two cases), Bearer only for a browser navigation; an API
#          token as the Basic password resolves to its owner. /api/v1/auth/me
#          and /api/v1/repositories keep refusing the token-as-Basic.
#   #4550  An admin's repository-scoped API token could read
#          /api/v1/admin/stats and /api/v1/admin/downloads* (client IPs, users,
#          paths of every repository). Fixed: 403, like /admin/holds/*.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (FIX)     anonymous private -> 401 + Basic + Bearer; anonymous missing ->
#             the same status, challenges and body; Accept: text/html -> 401
#             Bearer only; `-u x:<token>` -> 200 with the bytes; curl --anyauth
#             (credentials only after a challenge) -> 200; both downloads land
#             in download_statistics under the token owner; the repo-scoped
#             admin token gets 403 on stats, downloads, downloads/by-user and
#             downloads/by-ip.
#   (CONTROL) on both images: anonymous public download 200; Bearer token
#             download 200; valid-but-not-entitled 404; token-as-Basic 401 on
#             /auth/me and /repositories; unrestricted admin token 200 on stats
#             and downloads and sees the owner's attributed download; scoped
#             token 403 on /admin/holds/summary (pre-existing #4273).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~30 back-to-back calls including Basic attempts.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
